Math.rint, Math.round and Math.ulp(double) as Java defines them: the fixes
TeaVM made after 0.16.0, in its commits 570a7eea4 and 11a50bc0b.

rint was round's long as a double: half away from zero (rint(2.5) was 3.0),
a zero without its sign (rint(-0.3) was 0.0), and Long.MAX_VALUE past 2^63
(rint(1e300)); round added a half and truncated, which rounds
0.49999999999999994 to 1 and odd integers past 2^52 up; ulp masked the
exponent with 0xEFF0... for 0x7FF0..., so that ulp(1.0) was 2^-308, not 2^-52.

